{"name":"Cigar Smoke","hex":"#78857a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cigar smoke","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Smoke that comes from a cigar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cigar_smoke"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cigar","blocks":[{"text":"A cigar is a rolled bundle of dried and fermented tobacco leaves made to be smoked. Cigars are produced in a variety of sizes and shapes. Since the 20th century, almost all cigars are made of three distinct components: the filler, the binder leaf which holds the filler together, and a wrapper leaf, which is often the highest quality leaf used. Often there will be a cigar band printed with the cigar manufacturer's logo. Modern cigars can come with two or more bands, especially Cuban cigars, showing Limited Edition bands displaying the year of production."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Cigar_tube_and_cutter.jpg/330px-Cigar_tube_and_cutter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cigar"},{"title":"Smoke","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke is an aerosol emitted when a material undergoes combustion or pyrolysis, together with the quantity of air that is entrained or otherwise mixed into the mass. It is commonly an unwanted by-product of fires, but may also be used for pest control (fumigation), communication, defensive and offensive capabilities in the military, cooking, or smoking. It is used in rituals where incense, sage, or resin is burned to produce a smell for spiritual or magical purposes. It can also be a flavoring agent and preservative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg/330px-Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG/500px-MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG/1280px-MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG/500px-MuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Indigenous tobacco pipe on display at the regional museum in San Andrés Tuxtla, Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuseoRegionalTuxtla_27.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1b/Harrynelsonpillsbury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1b/Harrynelsonpillsbury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Harry Nelson Pillsbury smoking a cigar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarrynelsonpillsbury.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Ybor_Cigar_workers.jpg/500px-Ybor_Cigar_workers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Ybor_Cigar_workers.jpg/500px-Ybor_Cigar_workers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inside an Ybor City cigar factory c. 1920","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYbor_Cigar_workers.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Cigar_making_display%2C_Ybor_City_Museum_State_Park%2C_Tampa%2C_Florida.jpg/500px-Cigar_making_display%2C_Ybor_City_Museum_State_Park%2C_Tampa%2C_Florida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Cigar_making_display%2C_Ybor_C